            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention refers to a method for transmitting data using a collision-resistant full-duplex communication protocol over a half-duplex connection. The method comprises the method steps: ending a data reception mode for a first device (250) transmitting the data; transmitting, by the first device (250), a data frame over the half-duplex connection for receipt by a second device (108); monitoring, by the first device (250), for an acknowledgement from the second device (108), the acknowledgement comprising a cyclic redundancy check value; determining that the data frame needs to be retransmitted; identifying a device role of the first device (250); and retransmitting the data frame at a time according to the identification of the device role.</p>
            </abstract>
